# YouTube Downloader — environment (single .env.local drives the VPS deploy).
# Copy to .env.local and fill in:  cp .env.local.example .env.local

# ── YouTube cookies (optional but recommended) ────────────────────────────────
# Netscape-format cookies for YouTube so downloads bypass bot detection.
#
# Preferred: store the exported Netscape cookies.txt at ~/.yt_cookie.txt on the
# VPS. deploy.sh copies it into the app at deploy time, and app.py falls back to
# the same path when run standalone. Override the path with YOUTUBE_COOKIES_FILE.
#
# Alternatively, paste the raw Netscape block (one line) here:
# YOUTUBE_COOKIES=
#
# Full precedence (highest first):
#   YOUTUBE_COOKIES (inline block)  >  YOUTUBE_COOKIES_FILE (path)  >  ~/.yt_cookie.txt
# YOUTUBE_COOKIES_FILE=
# COOKIES_FILE=

# ── Port (optional, default 7860) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Must match the Cloudflare Tunnel rule.  Leave default unless 7860 is taken.
# PORT=7860

# ── Bind address (optional, default 0.0.0.0) ──────────────────────────────────
# deploy.sh sets HOST=127.0.0.1 so the VPS answers only the Cloudflare Tunnel.
# Leave unset for Docker/Render/Hugging Face, which need 0.0.0.0 to be reachable.
# HOST=127.0.0.1
